    "notes": [
      "SD_MODE: driven low = shutdown; high = left channel; pull-up through RSMALL (kΩ) = 94.0 x VDDIO - 100 (210 kΩ at 3.3 V) = right; through RLARGE = 222.2 x VDDIO - 100 (634 kΩ at 3.3 V) = (left + right) / 2. If VDDIO can exceed VDD, add ~2 kΩ in series when driving it high.",
      "GAIN_SLOT open = 9 dB; to GND = 12 dB; 100 kΩ to GND = 15 dB; to VDD = 6 dB; 100 kΩ to VDD = 3 dB. Do not change it while audio plays.",
      "No MCLK needed: BCLK, LRCLK and DIN from the controller (ESP32, RP2040, Pi). LRCLK only at 8, 16, 32, 44.1, 48, 88.2 or 96 kHz; never stop LRCLK while BCLK runs.",
      "Filterless bridge-tied output: the speaker between OUTP and OUTN (never to ground), speaker inductance > 10 µH; short wide output and supply traces, ferrite beads on long speaker leads."
    ],
    "page": "Typical application circuits; Table 5 SD_MODE control, Table 6 SD_MODE pull-up values, Table 8 gain selection; power-supply input (p. 33)"
  },
